---js
{
  eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true,
  pagination: {
    data: "embed_registry",
    size: 1,
    alias: "entry",
    // Each entry’s data comes from its own org’s file in _data/embed_figures/.
    // Stop the build on an entry with no matching org, type or metric, rather
    // than build a card from missing (or another org’s) data.
    before(entries, data) {
      const sections = { tile: "figures", comparison: "comparisons", headline: "headlines", trend: "trends" };
      for (const { org, type, metric } of entries) {
        if (!data.embed_figures[org]?.[sections[type]]?.[metric]) {
          throw new Error(`embed_registry.json entry "${org}/${type}/${metric}" has no matching data in _data/embed_figures/${org}.json`);
        }
      }
      return entries;
    }
  },
  permalink: "embed/f/{{ entry.org }}/{{ entry.type }}/{{ entry.metric }}/"
}
---
{#- One bare card per entry in embed_registry.json (GH#4005): org, type and
    metric together pick a card type and a data key, so we control what that
    combination shows without Gates changing anything on their page. The
    loader fetches this fragment and drops it straight into the custom
    element’s shadow root — no doctype, head, or body, just the card. -#}
{%- from "system/component.njk" import component -%}
{%- set data = embed_figures[entry.org] -%}
{%- set org = data.org -%}
{%- set asOf = data.source.retrieved -%}
{#- A stable per-entry string for this card’s internal element IDs (popover
    targets, headings) — not shown anywhere, just needs to be unique. -#}
{%- set entryId = entry.org ~ "_" ~ entry.type ~ "_" ~ entry.metric -%}
{#- Every card’s attribution link defaults to the OA.Report landing page and
    carries the org’s own report as a swappable alternative; the snippet’s
    placeholder div sets data-oareport-link="report" to ask the loader to
    swap to it.
    This is a setting on the snippet, not the registry, so it applies to any
    entry without changing what’s built here. -#}
{%- set attributionUrl = "https://oa.report" -%}
{%- if entry.type == "tile" -%}
{{ component("embed/tile", { id: entryId, figure: data.figures[entry.metric], org: org, asOf: asOf, attributionUrl: attributionUrl, attributionAltUrl: org.report_url, headingLevel: 2 }) }}
{%- elif entry.type == "comparison" -%}
{{ component("embed/comparison", { id: entryId, comparison: data.comparisons[entry.metric], org: org, asOf: asOf, attributionUrl: attributionUrl, attributionAltUrl: org.report_url, headingLevel: 2 }) }}
{%- elif entry.type == "headline" -%}
{{ component("embed/headline", { id: entryId, headline: data.headlines[entry.metric], org: org, asOf: asOf, attributionUrl: attributionUrl, attributionAltUrl: org.report_url, headingLevel: 2 }) }}
{%- elif entry.type == "trend" -%}
{{ component("embed/trend", { id: entryId, trend: data.trends[entry.metric], org: org, asOf: asOf, attributionUrl: attributionUrl, attributionAltUrl: org.report_url, headingLevel: 2 }) }}
{%- endif -%}
